[center]
[size=6][b][color=#D6A24A]CIGAR[/color][/b][/size]
[size=4][b]Contextual Interactions for Skyrim[/b][/size]
[/center]

[size=4][b][color=#D6A24A]Description[/color][/b][/size]

[color=#D4D4D8]
CIGAR is an ESP-less SKSE plugin. It shows a SkyPrompt prompt when an action makes sense; one key completes it. Each module has its own switch. Other mods' integrations are detected at runtime and stay inactive when those mods are absent. CIGAR includes none of their files.
[/color]

[size=4][b][color=#D6A24A]What CIGAR Does[/color][/b][/size]

[color=#D4D4D8]
[b]Daily life:[/b] rest, pass time, eat, drink, bathe, change clothes and observe your surroundings.
[b]Gear and quests:[/b] equip useful finds, read books, remove or put on a helmet, recharge weapons, apply poison, track quests and swap outfits with a mannequin.
[b]Combat:[/b] choose ranged or melee weapons, use Throw, and show prompts for Lock On, Grapple, Execute and Surrender when their mods are installed.
[b]Squeeze Past:[/b] hold the prompt to slip past a standing or walking person blocking your way. It temporarily changes the player's collision group, leaving the NPC's collision in place. It does not target enemies or someone talking to you. This needs your own EVG Animated Traversal and Offset Movement Animation installations. CIGAR prepares its gesture from your EVG clip; it ships no animation from those mods. Without EVG, Squeeze Past is off.

Most non-combat prompts fill a hold ring, so a tap does nothing. Double-tap to dismiss a prompt until the situation changes. Combat actions use a single press. Potions use a ring outside combat and a single press in combat. Squeeze Past acts immediately while held. Pass Time and Lean have their own switches in the CIGAR panel, apart from Sit and Lie Down.

Prompts are in English or Korean. In third person they appear ahead of your character's head; in first person they stay on your character. The settings panel lets you change their third-person offset.

The full prompt list and settings are in [b]README.md[/b] in the download.
[/color]

[size=4][b][color=#D6A24A]Installation[/color][/b][/size]

[color=#D4D4D8]
1. Install SKSE64, Address Library for SKSE Plugins and SkyPrompt with its own requirements.
2. Install CIGAR with MO2 or Vortex.
3. Launch Skyrim through SKSE. No new game is needed.

The four prompt keys default to 1–4. The Keys page also supports the D-pad and middle or side mouse buttons. Gamepad behavior was checked with one Xbox controller.
[/color]

[size=4][b][color=#D6A24A]Requirements[/color][/b][/size]

[color=#D4D4D8]
[b]Required[/b]
- Skyrim Special Edition / Anniversary Edition / VR. The same DLL targets SE, AE and VR; the player release was tested on Skyrim 1.6.1170.
- [url=https://skse.silverlock.org/]SKSE64[/url]
- [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/32444]Address Library for SKSE Plugins[/url]
- [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/148703]SkyPrompt[/url] (tested with 2.4.0 and 2.3.15)
- [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/120352]SKSE Menu Framework[/url] and ImGui Icons, required by SkyPrompt. Menu Framework also hosts CIGAR's settings panel.

[b]Optional integrations[/b] — detected at runtime; install only the prompts you want:
- [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/135288]Bathing in Skyrim - Renewed[/url]
- Survival Mode and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/78244]Survival Mode Improved - SKSE[/url]; [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/96876]Gourmet[/url] for food classification
- [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/51614]True Directional Movement[/url]; Grapple by Smooth (Patreon); [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/64741]Valhalla Combat[/url]
- [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/108159]Acheron[/url] and [url=https://www.loverslab.com/files/file/23123-yamete-kudasai/]Yamete Kudasai[/url] (LoversLab)
- [url=https://www.loverslab.com/files/file/39023-private-needs-orgasm/]Private Needs - Orgasm[/url] (LoversLab); Fill Her Up Baka Edition (LoversLab / SubscribeStar); [url=https://www.loverslab.com/files/file/17496-babodialogue/]BaboDialogue[/url] (LoversLab)
- [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/14890]The Wizard Warrior[/url]
- Squeeze Past: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/63232]EVG Animated Traversal[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/110408]Offset Movement Animation[/url] and Open Animation Replacer for its gesture
- SexLab or OStim for scene-aware prompt suppression

These are separate downloads. CIGAR does not ship their files. It works without the optional integrations.
[/color]

[size=4][b][color=#D6A24A]Known Issues and Support[/color][/b][/size]

[color=#D4D4D8]
- Third-person prompts can stay at the player position if the update hook stops reaching CIGAR. CIGAR logs the stalled hook; the underlying cause is not fixed yet.
- Throw may refuse until the first death after loading a game. Execute may miss its first press.
- The Wizard Warrior's enchantment remains after End Wizard Warrior until it expires, as that mod is designed to do.

For a problem report, include your Skyrim and SKSE versions, steps to reproduce it and [b]Documents/My Games/Skyrim Special Edition/SKSE/CIGAR.log[/b]. Routine blocked-prompt diagnostics go to that log; a broken integration or failed action still gives a HUD notice when needed.
[/color]

